522
00:44:30.480 --> 00:44:31.470
So...

523
00:44:32.560 --> 00:44:34.597
You never had a long-term relationship?

524
00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:37.115
No. Not unless we count you.

525
00:44:39.480 --> 00:44:42.359
Is it possible that you could've had a kid
without knowing it?

526
00:44:42.440 --> 00:44:43.430
N0.

527
00:44:45.360 --> 00:44:47.237
- Then how do you explain--
- Danny.

528
00:44:50.280 --> 00:44:51.315
All right?

529
00:45:02.400 --> 00:45:03.993
Thank you, by the way.

530
00:45:05.360 --> 00:45:06.395
For?

531
00:45:06.480 --> 00:45:09.120
For leaving Baron's apartment
so I wouldn't be a target.

532
00:45:11.160 --> 00:45:13.834
Corning to get me in Georgia
when you could've just run for your life.

533
00:45:14.880 --> 00:45:18.191
I just wanted to put you
on a private plane

534
00:45:18.280 --> 00:45:20.396
and give you a free trip to Hungary.

535
00:45:21.720 --> 00:45:23.279
Where I'm gonna find...

536
00:45:23.760 --> 00:45:25.319
Hungarians.

537
00:45:27.280 --> 00:45:28.395
Right.

538
00:45:32.560 --> 00:45:33.789
When I saw him...

539
00:45:35.960 --> 00:45:37.678
it was like I was seeing a ghost.

540
00:45:39.600 --> 00:45:40.999
A ghost with a gun.

541
00:45:43.320 --> 00:45:46.676
Like... every trigger I've ever pulled.

542
00:46:18.760 --> 00:46:21.912
I told you to stay in Colombia
and await orders.

543
00:46:24.640 --> 00:46:26.074
I wanted to talk to you.

544
00:46:40.240 --> 00:46:41.753
He's very good.

545
00:46:42.880 --> 00:46:44.109
He's the best.

546
00:46:44.880 --> 00:46:46.393
That's why I sent you.

547
00:46:49.320 --> 00:46:52.950
He knew every move of mine
before I made it.

548
00:46:54.360 --> 00:46:58.035
I'd have him, right there,
and I'd take the shot...

549
00:46:58.840 --> 00:47:01.036
and he'd be gone.

550
00:47:03.120 --> 00:47:04.315
Like a ghost.

551
00:47:05.400 --> 00:47:07.118
Did you get a look at his face?

552
00:47:08.440 --> 00:47:09.475
Not really.

553
00:47:09.560 --> 00:47:13.030
I saw him up the stairs,
through a dirty mirror.

554
00:47:13.120 --> 00:47:14.474
I thought you were on the roof.

555
00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:17.556
I was. He got a line on me.
I had tojump down.

556
00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:19.119
What do we always drill?

557
00:47:20.040 --> 00:47:21.314
You hold the high ground.

558
00:47:21.440 --> 00:47:24.478
You put his back against the wall,
and you don't let him go.

559
00:47:26.120 --> 00:47:27.235
I know that.

560
00:47:30.880 --> 00:47:32.678
The whole thing was weird.

561
00:47:33.040 --> 00:47:34.633
It was... wiggy.

562
00:47:35.360 --> 00:47:36.350
How?

563
00:47:37.400 --> 00:47:41.394
I don't know,
it was as if I were watching it all.

564
00:47:42.560 --> 00:47:43.789
Who is he?

565
00:47:45.080 --> 00:47:47.435
Junior, this thing
that you're struggling with,

566
00:47:47.520 --> 00:47:50.114
this strangeness, it's fear.

567
00:47:51.280 --> 00:47:52.429
Don't hate it.

568
00:47:53.280 --> 00:47:54.509
Lean into it.

569
00:47:55.120 --> 00:47:57.589
Embrace it and then overcome it.

570
00:47:57.680 --> 00:48:01.310
You are right on the threshold, son.

571
00:48:03.400 --> 00:48:04.515
This close.

572
00:48:08.680 --> 00:48:09.795
You hungry?

573
00:48:12.680 --> 00:48:13.750
Yes, sir.

574
00:48:14.760 --> 00:48:16.478
Bowl of cereal sound good?

575
00:48:19.040 --> 00:48:20.030
Yes, sir.

576
00:48:44.200 --> 00:48:45.190
G0!

577
00:49:13.360 --> 00:49:14.350
Grenade!

578
00:49:23.720 --> 00:49:26.109
Thank you! That's it! Back up!

579
00:49:29.520 --> 00:49:31.591
Hurry up! Everybody back to one.

580
00:49:31.680 --> 00:49:33.034
Everybody back to one.

581
00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:36.832
Back to one! Let's go!

582
00:49:45.600 --> 00:49:47.750
- Lots of new faces.
- Yep.

583
00:49:48.800 --> 00:49:51.269
They'll be the first boots
on the ground in Yemen.

584
00:49:52.800 --> 00:49:54.791
Do they understand
the rules of engagement,

585
00:49:54.880 --> 00:49:57.918
orjust, whatever moves, they shoot it?

586
00:49:58.960 --> 00:50:01.395
They're elite. They're disciplined.

587
00:50:02.360 --> 00:50:04.158
And if they get a clean shot
at their target

588
00:50:04.240 --> 00:50:06.436
through an apartment window,
they'll take it.

589
00:50:08.440 --> 00:50:11.114
You should think about that
on your way to Budapest.

590
00:50:13.400 --> 00:50:14.879
Henry's just landed there.

591
00:50:16.960 --> 00:50:18.280
You're moving out.

592
00:50:37.560 --> 00:50:38.595
Aniko?

593
00:50:41.000 --> 00:50:42.195
Thank you for your time.

594
00:50:43.920 --> 00:50:45.035
Here are the samples.

595
00:50:51.280 --> 00:50:54.079
This I can do for you in two days.

596
00:50:58.480 --> 00:50:59.959
This I need in two hours.

597
00:51:04.720 --> 00:51:05.869
We got a meeting with Yuri.

598
00:51:06.640 --> 00:51:08.119
He agreed to sit with us.

599
00:51:09.280 --> 00:51:10.315
You all right?

600
00:51:12.200 --> 00:51:14.157
I think I know
why he's as good as you, Henry.

601
00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:17.869
He is you.

602
00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:21.035
What?

603
00:51:22.120 --> 00:51:24.839
There's a DNA lab here.
I gave them samples.

604
00:51:26.160 --> 00:51:27.992
Yours and the baseball cap he was wearing.

605
00:51:29.720 --> 00:51:32.792
He looked so much like you,
I thought he had to be your son, so I...

606
00:51:35.320 --> 00:51:36.799
They did three tests.

607
00:51:36.880 --> 00:51:38.314
Your DNA and his.

608
00:51:39.640 --> 00:51:41.233
All three came back identical.

609
00:51:42.320 --> 00:51:43.879
Not close. Identical.

610
00:51:44.920 --> 00:51:46.274
As in "the same person."

611
00:51:49.560 --> 00:51:50.994
He's your clone.

612
00:51:53.800 --> 00:51:56.269
They thought I'd made a mistake,
given them samples of the same person,

613
00:51:56.360 --> 00:51:57.475
but I didn't.

614
00:51:59.240 --> 00:52:00.514
He is you.

615
00:52:01.160 --> 00:52:02.673
How's that even possible?

616
00:52:02.760 --> 00:52:04.478
It's complicated, but it's doable.

617
00:52:05.080 --> 00:52:07.594
All you'd really need is
a surrogate mother and a DNA sample.

618
00:52:07.680 --> 00:52:09.796
If they could clone a person,

619
00:52:09.880 --> 00:52:13.475
you'd think they'd clone
more doctors or scientists,

620
00:52:13.560 --> 00:52:15.437
not me.

621
00:52:15.520 --> 00:52:16.954
They could've cloned Nelson Mandela.

622
00:52:17.040 --> 00:52:19.350
Nelson Mandela couldn't kill a man
on a moving train

623
00:52:19.440 --> 00:52:20.874
from two kilometers away.

624
00:52:40.680 --> 00:52:41.715
Yuri.

625
00:52:45.240 --> 00:52:46.389
Mr. Brogan.

626
00:52:57.840 --> 00:52:59.717
Before we begin, I must confess,

627
00:52:59.800 --> 00:53:02.360
I have admired your work for many years.

628
00:53:03.480 --> 00:53:06.757
Wait. So you know who I am?

629
00:53:07.960 --> 00:53:10.031
A longtime listener, first-time caller,

630
00:53:10.120 --> 00:53:11.599
as they say in your country.

631
00:53:13.600 --> 00:53:17.070
I would congratulate you
on your retirement,

632
00:53:17.160 --> 00:53:21.119
but your last job has loose ends, yes?

633
00:53:21.200 --> 00:53:23.794
Yeah, well, my government lied to me
then tried to kill me,

634
00:53:23.880 --> 00:53:24.915
if that's what you mean.

635
00:53:25.000 --> 00:53:26.070
Yes.

636
00:53:26.160 --> 00:53:29.073
In Russia, we call that "Tuesday."

637
00:53:29.160 --> 00:53:32.152
But Americans, it hurts your feelings.

638
00:53:33.840 --> 00:53:34.750
So...

639
00:53:34.840 --> 00:53:37.309
So why was Dormov
trying to go back to Russia

640
00:53:37.440 --> 00:53:38.999
and why was I sent to kill him?

641
00:53:39.080 --> 00:53:41.993
Yes, down to business. Very American.

642
00:53:42.520 --> 00:53:44.033
You are a busy man.

643
00:53:45.840 --> 00:53:48.514
We were both friends with Jack.

644
00:53:48.600 --> 00:53:49.954
He was a good man.

645
00:53:50.920 --> 00:53:53.230
I'm mourning his death, like you.

646
00:53:53.800 --> 00:53:57.236
But the reason you are here
and I have not killed you...

647
00:53:58.120 --> 00:53:59.110
yet...

648
00:53:59.720 --> 00:54:02.030
is we share a common enemy.

649
00:54:02.840 --> 00:54:04.114
Clay Verris.

650
00:54:05.760 --> 00:54:08.434
He lured Dormov to the West,
funded his lab.

651
00:54:10.160 --> 00:54:12.310
And now you have met
the fruits of their labor.

652
00:54:12.880 --> 00:54:15.235
Dolly the sheep was cloned in '96.

653
00:54:15.320 --> 00:54:17.960
- But in '95--
- I was the sheep.

654
00:54:18.040 --> 00:54:19.838
Take it as a compliment.

655
00:54:19.920 --> 00:54:21.672
And you are the only one.

656
00:54:22.160 --> 00:54:26.358
With your DNA,
Verris raised the boy as his own son,

657
00:54:26.440 --> 00:54:29.080
trained him to be the perfect assassin.

658
00:54:30.440 --> 00:54:32.477
So why was Dormov trying to leave?

659
00:54:32.560 --> 00:54:34.597
For years, we tried to lure him back.

660
00:54:34.680 --> 00:54:35.954
Nothing.

661
00:54:36.040 --> 00:54:38.270
Then last year, they had a falling out.

662
00:54:38.360 --> 00:54:40.590
Dormov got scared, reached out to me.

663
00:54:40.680 --> 00:54:41.670
So, I--

664
00:54:41.760 --> 00:54:44.195
That still doesn't explain
why I was sent to kill him.

665
00:54:45.880 --> 00:54:48.679
We have indications
Dormov made a breakthrough.

666
00:54:49.400 --> 00:54:51.357
Modified human DNA.

667
00:54:51.440 --> 00:54:53.238
A path to mass production.

668
00:54:53.760 --> 00:54:56.832
But Dormov wanted soldiers
to be stronger, smarter.

669
00:54:57.280 --> 00:54:58.509
Verris...

670
00:54:59.840 --> 00:55:01.433
Verris wanted something else.

671
00:55:03.720 --> 00:55:05.040
What something else?

672
00:55:05.520 --> 00:55:06.669
Mr. Brogan,

673
00:55:07.080 --> 00:55:09.276
you are the best at what you do.

674
00:55:10.240 --> 00:55:13.676
But still you get tired.
You have fears, doubts.

675
00:55:13.760 --> 00:55:16.115
You feel pain, perhaps remorse.

676
00:55:17.440 --> 00:55:18.714
You have a conscience.

677
00:55:19.720 --> 00:55:21.677
This makes you human,

678
00:55:21.760 --> 00:55:23.831
but suboptimal as a soldier.

679
00:55:24.360 --> 00:55:25.873
Less than perfect.

680
00:55:26.360 --> 00:55:27.919
Less profitable.

681
00:55:31.080 --> 00:55:34.232
Clayton Verris is playing God with DNA.

682
00:55:35.440 --> 00:55:36.999
He must be stopped.

683
00:55:39.000 --> 00:55:41.276
If it's that dangerous,
why not send a missile?

684
00:55:41.840 --> 00:55:43.239
Blow up his lab.

685
00:55:44.240 --> 00:55:45.753
That is what we're doing.

686
00:55:46.520 --> 00:55:50.195
Except you are the missile.

687
00:55:51.600 --> 00:55:53.034
I wish you luck.

688
00:55:55.480 --> 00:55:56.879
One last thing.

689
00:55:56.960 --> 00:55:59.679
Your escape from home two days ago?

690
00:56:00.880 --> 00:56:02.678
Amazing work.

691
00:56:02.760 --> 00:56:04.671
I was on the edge of my seat.

692
00:56:06.040 --> 00:56:07.269
Wait. What?

693
00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:09.559
How the hell do you know about that?

694
00:56:11.360 --> 00:56:14.034
I'm a big fan. What can I say?

695
00:56:19.160 --> 00:56:21.629
<i>/f even ha/f of when' he is saying is true,</i>

696
00:56:21.720 --> 00:56:23.199
we gotta talk to this kid.

697
00:56:23.280 --> 00:56:25.237
You're not gonna be safe until you do.

698
00:56:25.360 --> 00:56:27.715
So you think
if your 50-year-old self showed up

699
00:56:27.800 --> 00:56:30.155
and told you you were her clone,
that would make you calmer?

700
00:56:30.280 --> 00:56:31.076
Fifty-one.

701
00:56:31.800 --> 00:56:33.473
- What?
- Just saying.

702
00:56:34.640 --> 00:56:35.710
You know you're 51, Henry?

703
00:56:35.800 --> 00:56:37.359
-L'm rounding.
- Right.

704
00:56:38.240 --> 00:56:40.390
He's the mirror
you don't want to look into, Henry.

705
00:56:41.440 --> 00:56:43.511
But he's our best shot
at getting to Verris.

706
00:56:52.760 --> 00:56:53.875
Janet Lassiter?

707
00:56:54.800 --> 00:56:56.074
Who wants to know?

708
00:56:56.480 --> 00:56:59.677
Got a message for you, ma'am,
from a man who transferred $1,000

709
00:56:59.760 --> 00:57:01.956
into my Feathercoin account
just to make sure you got it.

710
00:57:02.560 --> 00:57:04.278
Does this person have a name?

711
00:57:04.920 --> 00:57:07.196
His name is
"$1,000 Into My Feathercoin Account."

712
00:57:09.880 --> 00:57:10.870
"Hello, Janet.

713
00:57:10.960 --> 00:57:13.600
Before you try to kill rne again,
consider this:

714
00:57:13.680 --> 00:57:16.877
Your home address is 1362 Carrol Grove.

715
00:57:16.960 --> 00:57:19.600
The security alarm code is 1776.

716
00:57:19.960 --> 00:57:22.110
You awaken at 6:12 every morning

717
00:57:22.200 --> 00:57:25.591
and stop for your decaf soy latte
with an extra shot by 6:42.

718
00:57:26.360 --> 00:57:28.954
Every night you stand
in front of your huge living room window,

719
00:57:29.040 --> 00:57:31.031
sipping a Jose Cuervo margarita,

720
00:57:31.120 --> 00:57:33.191
<i>with Forensic Files on the TV,</i>

721
00:57:33.640 --> 00:57:36.109
wearing your nice, comfy sweatpants."

722
00:57:41.200 --> 00:57:42.235
This is Lassiter.

723
00:57:42.320 --> 00:57:44.709
<i>There are shooters at your fen and two.</i>

724
00:57:44.800 --> 00:57:47.553
<i>Gel up ofi' 0f that chair,
you w/Y/ be AMF'ed.</i>

725
00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:50.517
Now, if I thought
the world needed another me,

726
00:57:50.600 --> 00:57:51.635
I would've had a kid.

727
00:57:52.880 --> 00:57:54.951
The program predates
my arrival at the Agency.

728
00:57:55.040 --> 00:57:56.030
You must know that.

729
00:57:56.160 --> 00:57:59.437
Yeah, perfect DC answer:
Something goes wrong, duck!

730
00:58:00.760 --> 00:58:02.273
Tip the bike guy.

731
00:58:03.200 --> 00:58:04.474
You can go.

732
00:58:05.360 --> 00:58:08.637
<i>Now, /ha ve your agent with me
against her will.</i>

733
00:58:09.080 --> 00:58:11.117
Danielle Zakarewski.

734
00:58:11.200 --> 00:58:12.429
She wants to come in.

735
00:58:13.400 --> 00:58:14.390
<i>Fine.</i>

736
00:58:14.480 --> 00:58:16.517
Like me, she is a patriot.

737
00:58:17.120 --> 00:58:20.795
Unlike me, she still wants to spend
the next couple decades

738
00:58:20.880 --> 00:58:22.951
scoring touchdowns for you assholes.

739
00:58:23.840 --> 00:58:25.877
Her safety is nonnegotiable.

740
00:58:26.440 --> 00:58:28.431
<i>Ten and two, Janet.</i>

741
00:58:28.520 --> 00:58:30.557
Decaf soy latte
with an extra shot for Janet.

742
00:58:30.640 --> 00:58:32.438
<i>The only person / '// tum her 0 ver f0</i>

743
00:58:32.520 --> 00:58:34.750
is the guy you sent after me in Cartagena.

744
00:58:35.280 --> 00:58:37.510
Don't even think
about sending anybody else.

745
00:58:37.600 --> 00:58:40.240
Family reunion. Very sweet.

746
00:58:40.600 --> 00:58:41.715
Yeah. Keep it up.

747
00:58:41.800 --> 00:58:44.030
You'll be the first person
I ever killed for free.

748
00:58:44.760 --> 00:58:46.751
How quickly can you get him to Budapest?

749
00:58:48.480 --> 00:58:49.709
<i>Five minutes ?</i>

750
00:58:52.640 --> 00:58:53.675
Good.

751
00:58:54.320 --> 00:58:56.311
She'll be in the courtyard
of the Vajdahunyad Castle

752
00:58:56.400 --> 00:58:57.993
at midnight tonight.

753
00:58:58.080 --> 00:58:59.479
Enjoy your latte.

754
00:59:01.080 --> 00:59:02.479
What's AM F?

755
00:59:02.600 --> 00:59:03.999
"Adios, motherfucker."

756
00:59:05.160 --> 00:59:06.798
How the hell does he know we're here?

757
00:59:18.840 --> 00:59:20.399
This is gonna work, right?

758
00:59:21.480 --> 00:59:22.550
Yes.

759
00:59:23.200 --> 00:59:24.474
How do you know?

760
00:59:25.200 --> 00:59:27.350
I know his taste.

761
00:59:28.880 --> 00:59:30.553
Wait, are you saying
you're attracted to me?

762
00:59:31.640 --> 00:59:34.632
Me? Now? Hell, no.

763
00:59:34.720 --> 00:59:37.997
But the younger,
less-mature version, maybe.

764
00:59:44.680 --> 00:59:47.832
When I came for you in Georgia,

765
00:59:48.720 --> 00:59:50.472
I didn't have to think about that.

766
00:59:50.560 --> 00:59:52.198
It was instinct.

767
00:59:53.480 --> 00:59:55.073
He was born with that too.

768
00:59:56.200 --> 00:59:58.271
Besides, he wants me.

769
01:01:08.120 --> 01:01:09.155
Right.

770
01:01:16.440 --> 01:01:17.714
Lovely courtyard.

771
01:01:19.520 --> 01:01:20.999
I'm sorry, ma'am.

772
01:01:21.080 --> 01:01:23.549
Before we go any farther,
I'm gonna need you to strip.

773
01:01:25.480 --> 01:01:26.754
B99 your pardon?

774
01:01:27.760 --> 01:01:29.751
Need to be certain
you're not wearing a wire.

775
01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:34.673
Okay, first of all,

776
01:01:34.760 --> 01:01:35.830
"ma'am"?

777
01:01:36.800 --> 01:01:38.837
I was raised to respect my elders.

778
01:01:41.640 --> 01:01:43.199
Take your clothes off, please.

779
01:02:11.160 --> 01:02:12.434
Turn around, please.

780
01:02:42.360 --> 01:02:43.873
I see you like to be thorough.

781
01:02:45.320 --> 01:02:47.197
Caution has kept me alive.

782
01:02:51.720 --> 01:02:52.994
Call his burner.

783
01:03:01.720 --> 01:03:02.835
Thank you.

784
01:03:04.560 --> 01:03:05.914
<i>Brogan.</i>

785
01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:09.436
In 12 minutes, I'm putting two bullets
in the back of her head.

786
01:03:09.520 --> 01:03:11.750
<i>Your orders are f0 deliver her safe/y.</i>

787
01:03:11.840 --> 01:03:13.558
My orders are to kill you.

788
01:03:14.200 --> 01:03:17.318
Are you familiar with the Quartz Chamber
of the catacombs?

789
01:03:17.400 --> 01:03:21.075
<i>Negative. We're doing this
someplace visible, where loan see you.</i>

790
01:03:21.160 --> 01:03:22.753
Now you have 11 minutes.

791
01:03:26.160 --> 01:03:28.037
Get dressed. We're taking a ride.

792
01:03:41.080 --> 01:03:42.639
Cab was a smart move.

793
01:03:44.040 --> 01:03:45.189
Where are you from?

794
01:03:46.600 --> 01:03:48.273
Your formality, it's Southern.

795
01:03:54.080 --> 01:03:56.310
You know, if you're gonna use me as bait
and possibly murder me,

796
01:03:56.400 --> 01:03:58.869
then the least you can do
is indulge me in some conversation.

797
01:04:01.160 --> 01:04:02.719
Just outside Atlanta.

798
01:04:04.160 --> 01:04:05.639
You two have a lot in common.

799
01:04:06.680 --> 01:04:08.159
I doubt that.

800
01:04:08.280 --> 01:04:09.554
You'd be surprised.

801
01:04:11.720 --> 01:04:13.393
You know, I started following him too.

802
01:04:13.480 --> 01:04:14.629
Just like you're doing.

803
01:04:15.520 --> 01:04:16.840
Then I got to know him.

804
01:04:18.120 --> 01:04:19.952
He's got a big heart, like you.

805
01:04:21.960 --> 01:04:23.917
What do you know about my heart?

806
01:04:25.720 --> 01:04:27.233
I know that you have one.

807
01:04:28.840 --> 01:04:29.989
And I know that it's telling you

808
01:04:30.080 --> 01:04:32.230
that something about the job
you've been given isn't right.

809
01:04:32.800 --> 01:04:34.313
A job is a job, ma'am.

810
01:04:48.040 --> 01:04:49.951
I wonder how much you paid the custodian.

811
01:04:51.440 --> 01:04:52.430
Wow.

812
01:04:53.520 --> 01:04:54.590
Left.

813
01:04:57.680 --> 01:04:58.909
Undo the chain.

814
01:05:03.680 --> 01:05:04.829
Basement.

815
01:05:05.560 --> 01:05:07.198
You must really know the city.

816
01:05:07.280 --> 01:05:08.953
I watch a lot of Nat Geo.

817
01:05:09.040 --> 01:05:11.156
- It says "Off-Limits."
- Ma'am.

818
01:05:18.720 --> 01:05:20.950
Wonder how many people
are buried down here.

819
01:05:21.040 --> 01:05:22.269
Stand over there.

820
01:05:51.960 --> 01:05:52.950
Go.

821
01:05:55.320 --> 01:05:56.469
If you knock out all the lights,

822
01:05:56.560 --> 01:05:58.631
how are you gonna see
your own trip wire on the way out?

823
01:05:59.320 --> 01:06:01.675
A grenade is no joke.
I mean, I get the idea.

824
01:06:01.760 --> 01:06:05.230
Darkness neutralizes his biggest strength,
and close quarters favors you, right?

825
01:06:05.320 --> 01:06:07.675
I mean, he can't throw a grenade
without killing me too.

826
01:06:07.760 --> 01:06:09.592
But what if he tries gas?

827
01:06:09.680 --> 01:06:11.318
You know? Or some sort of sedative agent?

828
01:06:12.040 --> 01:06:14.714
Way ahead of me.
Gas mask and night vision. Very smart.

829
01:06:14.800 --> 01:06:16.518
- Over there.
- And zip ties!

830
01:06:16.600 --> 01:06:17.920
These must be for me.

831
01:06:18.480 --> 01:06:19.914
But can I ask you something?

832
01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:23.152
Would you actually stop talking
long enough for me to answer?

833
01:06:23.240 --> 01:06:24.753
How much do you know about him?

834
01:06:24.840 --> 01:06:26.558
Anybody tell you why they wanted him dead?

835
01:06:26.640 --> 01:06:27.630
Guy cracked.

836
01:06:27.720 --> 01:06:30.360
Killed eight ops in a single night
and his spotter.

837
01:06:30.440 --> 01:06:32.192
- That's what they told you?
- That's what he did.

838
01:06:32.280 --> 01:06:34.191
No. No, not exactly.

839
01:06:34.280 --> 01:06:37.113
I was there
the night all those operatives were hit.

840
01:06:37.200 --> 01:06:40.238
They'd been sent to kill him,
and me, by Gemini.

841
01:06:40.320 --> 01:06:42.789
And not that it matters,
but his spotter was shot in Virginia,

842
01:06:42.880 --> 01:06:44.871
and the rest of those men
went down in Savannah.

843
01:06:48.440 --> 01:06:51.193
Henry can shoot long-distance,
but he can't shoot that long.

844
01:06:55.600 --> 01:06:58.831
Come on. Just think.
Does that make any sense to you?

845
01:06:58.920 --> 01:07:00.399
Do you understand what I'm saying?

846
01:07:00.480 --> 01:07:01.470
It doesn't--

847
01:07:02.320 --> 01:07:03.515
Better.

848
01:07:03.600 --> 01:07:05.079
FUCK you!

849
01:08:06.760 --> 01:08:08.273
Get up. Go.

850
01:08:22.680 --> 01:08:23.829
Stay right there.

851
01:08:32.080 --> 01:08:33.673
- Thank you.
- Here.

852
01:08:34.240 --> 01:08:35.560
You know how to light one of those?

853
01:08:35.640 --> 01:08:36.869
Oh, Jesus, Henry.

854
01:08:44.640 --> 01:08:46.597
Hey, thanks for the tip on the grenade.

855
01:08:48.120 --> 01:08:49.918
You were talking to him the whole time.

856
01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:51.070
Yeah.

857
01:08:51.160 --> 01:08:53.720
You either search somebody or you don't.

858
01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:57.069
And for the record...

859
01:08:57.960 --> 01:08:59.598
I do not want to kill you.

860
01:09:00.440 --> 01:09:02.556
But I absolutely will if I have to.

861
01:09:04.320 --> 01:09:06.197
What did Clay Verris tell you about me?

862
01:09:08.440 --> 01:09:10.431
Okay. Well, let me tell you about him.

863
01:09:11.280 --> 01:09:13.635
Because I know Mr. Verris very well.

864
01:09:14.760 --> 01:09:15.989
How'd he start you?

865
01:09:16.080 --> 01:09:18.230
Hunting birds? Rabbit?

866
01:09:18.320 --> 01:09:20.231
About 12 years old, moved you up to deer?

867
01:09:21.080 --> 01:09:23.390
I'm guessing 19, 2O years old

868
01:09:23.480 --> 01:09:25.676
the first time he ordered you
to shoot a person.

869
01:09:27.240 --> 01:09:28.594
Any of this ringing true?

870
01:09:30.040 --> 01:09:31.189
Yeah.

871
01:09:31.280 --> 01:09:33.715
He told you to "lean into your fear,"

872
01:09:34.440 --> 01:09:38.832
because you were "a warrior, blessed
with great gifts to defend the weak."

873
01:09:40.880 --> 01:09:42.757
But he couldn't stop the noise...

874
01:09:43.800 --> 01:09:47.759
that secret part of you that always felt
a little different than everybody else.

875
01:09:49.000 --> 01:09:50.638
Part that felt like a weirdo.

876
01:09:51.840 --> 01:09:53.069
You don't know shit.

877
01:09:53.160 --> 01:09:55.549
Kid, I know you inside out and backwards.

878
01:09:56.960 --> 01:09:59.110
You're allergic to bees.
You hate cilantro.

879
01:09:59.200 --> 01:10:01.077
You always sneeze four times.

880
01:10:02.520 --> 01:10:04.158
Everybody hates cilantro.

881
01:10:05.480 --> 01:10:06.834
You're meticulous.

882
01:10:07.320 --> 01:10:09.675
Thorough. Disciplined. Relentless.

883
01:10:10.360 --> 01:10:11.680
You love puzzles.

884
01:10:13.040 --> 01:10:15.475
You're a chess player. Right?

885
01:10:16.240 --> 01:10:17.594
Good, too, I bet.

886
01:10:18.480 --> 01:10:20.596
But you suffer from insomnia.

887
01:10:21.040 --> 01:10:22.951
Your mind never lets you sleep.

888
01:10:23.040 --> 01:10:25.236
And even when it does,
it attacks you with nightmares.

889
01:10:25.320 --> 01:10:27.675
I'm talking 'bout those
three-o'clock-in-the-morning,

890
01:10:27.760 --> 01:10:30.354
somebody-please-save-me
kind of nightmares.

891
01:10:31.280 --> 01:10:34.318
And then there's the doubts,
and those are the worst.

892
01:10:34.400 --> 01:10:36.994
You hate 'em,
and you hate yourself for having 'em.

893
01:10:37.080 --> 01:10:38.673
They make you feel weak.

894
01:10:38.760 --> 01:10:41.195
A real soldier doesn't doubt, right?

895
01:10:42.560 --> 01:10:46.474
The only time you ever truly feel happy

896
01:10:46.560 --> 01:10:49.552
is when you're flat on your belly
about to squeeze a trigger.

897
01:10:50.400 --> 01:10:53.995
And in that moment,
the world makes perfect sense.

898
01:10:56.200 --> 01:10:57.793
How do you think I know all of that?

899
01:10:57.880 --> 01:10:59.996
I don't give a shit how you know anything.

900
01:11:00.080 --> 01:11:02.310
Look at me, dummy!

901
01:11:02.960 --> 01:11:04.280
Look at us!

902
01:11:05.080 --> 01:11:09.472
Twenty-five years ago, your father
took my blood and he cloned me.

903
01:11:09.560 --> 01:11:12.439
He made you from me.

904
01:11:12.520 --> 01:11:14.511
Our DNA is identical.

905
01:11:15.040 --> 01:11:16.633
He's telling you the truth.

906
01:11:16.720 --> 01:11:17.994
Shut up.

907
01:11:18.080 --> 01:11:20.310
He chose me
'cause there's never been anybody like me,

908
01:11:20.400 --> 01:11:23.711
and he knew one day I was gonna get old
and then you'd step in.

909
01:11:23.840 --> 01:11:26.116
He's been lying to you the whole time.

910
01:11:26.200 --> 01:11:28.111
He told you you were an orphan.

911
01:11:28.560 --> 01:11:30.756
And of all the people in the world
to come after me,

912
01:11:30.840 --> 01:11:31.955
why would he send you?

913
01:11:32.040 --> 01:11:33.314
Because I'm the best.

914
01:11:34.720 --> 01:11:36.950
You are obviously not the best.

915
01:11:39.600 --> 01:11:41.477
You got a hard-ass head.

916
01:11:43.440 --> 01:11:46.671
Guess this was supposed to be
your birthday or something.

917
01:11:46.760 --> 01:11:49.434
I had to die, and you had to do it.

918
01:11:49.520 --> 01:11:50.749
As long as I was alive,

919
01:11:50.840 --> 01:11:54.276
somehow Clay's little experiment
was incomplete.

920
01:11:54.360 --> 01:11:56.874
That's the maniac
you're pulling a trigger for.

921
01:11:57.000 --> 01:11:58.593
Shut your mouth about him.

922
01:11:59.200 --> 01:12:00.429
You're just trying to rattle me.

923
01:12:00.520 --> 01:12:02.158
I'm trying to save you!

924
01:12:04.040 --> 01:12:06.350
What are you, 23?

925
01:12:07.200 --> 01:12:08.520
Still a virgin, right?

926
01:12:09.160 --> 01:12:10.195
Yeah.

927
01:12:10.880 --> 01:12:13.235
Dying to be in a relationship and connect,

928
01:12:13.320 --> 01:12:15.834
but terrified to let anybody near you.

929
01:12:17.400 --> 01:12:21.598
Because what if
somebody actually saw who you are?

930
01:12:22.320 --> 01:12:23.719
How could they love you?

931
01:12:24.880 --> 01:12:26.951
So everyb0dy's just targets,

932
01:12:27.680 --> 01:12:29.159
and you're just a weapon.

933
01:12:32.080 --> 01:12:33.229
Hey. Hey!

934
01:13:00.400 --> 01:13:01.390
Hey!

935
01:13:19.760 --> 01:13:20.989
Don't shoot him!

936
01:13:38.840 --> 01:13:39.955
Don't shoot him!

937
01:14:33.160 --> 01:14:34.594
Don't! No!

938
01:14:34.680 --> 01:14:35.909
Drop it!

939
01:14:36.320 --> 01:14:37.799
Drop it! I will shoot you!

940
01:14:39.160 --> 01:14:40.309
No, you won't!

941
01:15:19.440 --> 01:15:21.192
Get your hands off of him!

942
01:15:22.600 --> 01:15:24.113
Let him go!

943
01:15:26.440 --> 01:15:27.555
Right now!

944
01:15:35.800 --> 01:15:37.029
I'm not you!

945
01:15:38.560 --> 01:15:39.709
You hear me, old man?

946
01:15:41.240 --> 01:15:42.674
I'm not you!

947
01:15:45.480 --> 01:15:47.835
- Where is he?
- He's gone.

948
01:15:47.920 --> 01:15:49.877
- Did you hit him?
- I think so, yeah.

949
01:15:50.720 --> 01:15:52.757
- Where?
- Shoulder, I think.

950
01:15:55.440 --> 01:15:56.714
Then he'll recover.

951
01:15:58.320 --> 01:15:59.549
Is that a good thing?

952
01:16:18.680 --> 01:16:23.277
You know, it's not every day you see
a guy get his ass kicked on two continents

953
01:16:23.360 --> 01:16:24.794
by himself.

954
01:16:32.120 --> 01:16:33.155
Where to?

955
01:16:34.240 --> 01:16:35.469
Georgia.

956
01:16:36.160 --> 01:16:37.673
It's where Verris is.

957
01:16:52.280 --> 01:16:53.270
Man.

958
01:16:55.120 --> 01:16:56.394
That poor kid.

959
01:16:57.520 --> 01:16:59.033
He must be terrified.

960
01:17:00.560 --> 01:17:03.359
And he's going home,
walking into a buzz saw.

961
01:17:09.160 --> 01:17:10.594
I need to get some sleep.

962
01:17:11.280 --> 01:17:12.350
You too.

963
01:17:13.960 --> 01:17:16.236
Not me. That's where the ghosts are.

964
01:17:17.560 --> 01:17:18.675
Sleep.

965
01:17:44.280 --> 01:17:45.475
Tell me something.

966
01:17:46.840 --> 01:17:49.400
Why is it so hard for you
to kill this man?

967
01:17:52.400 --> 01:17:56.155
You know how much I hate
Big Hammock Park, Pop?

968
01:17:57.920 --> 01:17:58.955
What?

969
01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:02.833
Ever since I was about 12 years old...

970
01:18:03.880 --> 01:18:07.635
we would shoot turkeys there
for my birthday.

971
01:18:09.800 --> 01:18:11.393
And I always hated it.

972
01:18:13.240 --> 01:18:14.389
But I was an orphan, right?

973
01:18:14.480 --> 01:18:17.950
So, how would we even know
when my birthday was?

974
01:18:19.960 --> 01:18:23.430
But you never seemed to notice,
so we just keep going.

975
01:18:23.520 --> 01:18:26.831
Okay, so, next year
we'll try Chuck E. Cheese.

976
01:18:28.680 --> 01:18:29.715
Yeah.

977
01:18:30.360 --> 01:18:32.237
You, me,

978
01:18:32.320 --> 01:18:35.073
and the lab guys who made me.

979
01:18:42.080 --> 01:18:43.070
Yeah.

980
01:18:46.800 --> 01:18:48.234
I...

981
01:18:50.520 --> 01:18:52.158
always believed...

982
01:18:54.120 --> 01:18:56.873
you'd be happier not knowing.

983
01:18:59.600 --> 01:19:00.715
Happy-

984
01:19:02.640 --> 01:19:04.278
You know when I'm happy, Pop?

985
01:19:05.840 --> 01:19:07.478
When I'm flat on my belly,

986
01:19:08.360 --> 01:19:10.158
about to squeeze a trigger.

987
01:19:12.560 --> 01:19:14.233
It's the only time I'm happy.

988
01:19:16.320 --> 01:19:18.630
And this wasn't even a mistake.

989
01:19:20.480 --> 01:19:22.232
It's not like you got someone pregnant

990
01:19:22.360 --> 01:19:25.716
and then had to man up and raise me.

991
01:19:25.800 --> 01:19:28.952
No, you made a decision

992
01:19:29.760 --> 01:19:33.833
to have a scientist make a person
out of another person.

993
01:19:33.920 --> 01:19:35.274
No, that's not what it was.

994
01:19:35.360 --> 01:19:37.158
That's exactly what it was.

995
01:19:38.520 --> 01:19:40.158
Then you sent me...

996
01:19:41.640 --> 01:19:42.675
t0 kill him.

997
01:19:42.760 --> 01:19:46.116
Of all the shooters in the world,
why would you send me?

998
01:19:46.200 --> 01:19:49.591
He's your darkness.
You had to walk through this on your own.

999
01:19:51.920 --> 01:19:53.479
Maybe you're my darkness.

1000
01:19:55.760 --> 01:19:58.229
That lie you told rne...

1001
01:19:59.920 --> 01:20:01.672
that my parents...

1002
01:20:03.000 --> 01:20:05.958
dumped me at a fire station.

1003
01:20:08.240 --> 01:20:09.594
And I believed that.

1004
01:20:11.480 --> 01:20:13.391
Do you know how that made me feel?

1005
01:20:13.480 --> 01:20:15.471
It was a necessary lie.

1006
01:20:15.560 --> 01:20:17.710
None of this shit is necessary!

1007
01:20:19.000 --> 01:20:21.196
You made a choice to do this to me.

1008
01:20:21.280 --> 01:20:24.159
Can't you see how not okay I am?

1009
01:20:24.240 --> 01:20:25.355
Bullshit!

1010
01:20:25.960 --> 01:20:28.349
You forget who you're talking to, Junior.

1011
01:20:28.440 --> 01:20:29.714
I've seen battle.

1012
01:20:30.320 --> 01:20:31.754
I've seen soldiers go over the edge

1013
01:20:31.840 --> 01:20:33.956
because more was being asked of them
than they could give.

1014
01:20:34.040 --> 01:20:35.599
That's not you.

1015
01:20:35.680 --> 01:20:38.069
Your world is stable and dependable.

1016
01:20:38.160 --> 01:20:39.480
I made sure of that.

1017
01:20:39.560 --> 01:20:42.234
You have something
that Henry himself never had.

1018
01:20:42.320 --> 01:20:46.314
You have a loving, dedicated,
present father,

1019
01:20:46.400 --> 01:20:50.075
who tells you every goddamn day
that you are precious and that you matter.

1020
01:20:50.160 --> 01:20:53.710
Jesus, the whole point of this thing
was to give you all of Henry's gifts

1021
01:20:53.800 --> 01:20:56.110
without his pain, and I did.

1022
01:20:57.120 --> 01:21:00.476
Don't doubt, Junior.

1023
01:21:02.760 --> 01:21:04.239
You're better than that.

1024
01:21:15.080 --> 01:21:16.115
Come here.

1025
01:21:21.560 --> 01:21:23.517
I love you, son.

1026
01:21:26.800 --> 01:21:29.314
Just don't let yourself down.

1027
01:21:58.360 --> 01:22:01.716
Like so many of my encounters,
it was short but sweet.

1028
01:22:02.200 --> 01:22:03.520
Thanks,baby.

1029
01:22:17.000 --> 01:22:18.798
There should be a truck here somewhere.

1030
01:22:28.200 --> 01:22:29.474
Don't move.

1031
01:22:34.920 --> 01:22:36.274
What was in that?

1032
01:22:36.360 --> 01:22:37.680
Bee venom.

1033
01:22:41.800 --> 01:22:43.757
No. No, you can't do that.

1034
01:22:44.880 --> 01:22:46.439
You can't do that. He's allergic!

1035
01:22:46.520 --> 01:22:48.397
Henry, can you breathe?

1036
01:22:48.840 --> 01:22:50.160
Henry, try to breathe.

1037
01:22:50.920 --> 01:22:52.354
- You okay?
- Please.

1038
01:22:52.440 --> 01:22:54.750
Henry. Henry, can you breathe?

1039
01:22:54.840 --> 01:22:55.910
Please!

1040
01:22:56.000 --> 01:22:58.196
Try to breathe. Henry! Henry!

1041
01:22:59.360 --> 01:23:00.430
Breathe!

1042
01:23:01.080 --> 01:23:02.957
- Why are you doing this?
- Come on, Henry.

1043
01:23:05.520 --> 01:23:08.717
- Why are you doing this?
- Henry. Henry, breathe. Come on!

1044
01:23:09.720 --> 01:23:10.710
Hey, he)'-

1045
01:23:11.240 --> 01:23:12.594
Breathe, Henry.

1046
01:23:23.560 --> 01:23:25.233
Epinephrine antihistamine.

1047
01:23:28.720 --> 01:23:29.869
You'll be fine.

1048
01:23:34.000 --> 01:23:35.070
I'm sorry.

1049
01:23:35.960 --> 01:23:37.359
I had to be sure.

1050
01:23:37.960 --> 01:23:39.439
No, it's all good.

1051
01:23:40.240 --> 01:23:42.595
This whole shit's been a little difficult.

1052
01:23:42.680 --> 01:23:44.591
I hate to break up the party,

1053
01:23:44.680 --> 01:23:46.910
but how the hell do you always know
where we are?

1054
01:23:49.360 --> 01:23:50.634
They're tracking you.

1055
01:23:54.040 --> 01:23:55.269
Do you trust me?

1056
01:24:18.960 --> 01:24:22.476
They chipped you...
during your surgery three years ago.

1057
01:24:27.320 --> 01:24:28.310
Verris.

1058
01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:31.434
You know him too?

1059
01:24:32.440 --> 01:24:34.750
Panama. Kuwait. Somalia.

1060
01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:37.034
Can you take us to him?

1061
01:24:39.400 --> 01:24:41.152
We need to shut him down.

1062
01:24:41.840 --> 01:24:42.955
Both of us.

1063
01:24:54.920 --> 01:24:56.638
You grew up in Philadelphia, right?

1064
01:24:57.080 --> 01:24:59.356
Yep. Place called "The Bottom."

1065
01:25:00.680 --> 01:25:01.875
The Bottom.

1066
01:25:03.840 --> 01:25:05.274
Tell me about my mother.

1067
01:25:08.360 --> 01:25:10.237
Helen Jackson Brogan.

1068
01:25:10.320 --> 01:25:12.755
Worked two jobs for 40 years.

1069
01:25:12.840 --> 01:25:15.150
That woman used to whup my ass.

1070
01:25:16.240 --> 01:25:19.039
- Did you deserve it?
- Usually.

1071
01:25:19.120 --> 01:25:21.191
Does being angry and stupid

1072
01:25:21.280 --> 01:25:24.318
and never really trying at anything
mean you deserve it?

1073
01:25:25.880 --> 01:25:29.236
Our father wasn't around much.
He left when I was five.

1074
01:25:29.320 --> 01:25:32.790
And I think every time she looked at me,
she just saw him, so...

1075
01:25:34.280 --> 01:25:35.998
I had to get the hell out of there.

1076
01:25:36.720 --> 01:25:38.040
Joined the corps.

1077
01:25:38.880 --> 01:25:41.235
First time I ever made any real friends.

1078
01:25:41.320 --> 01:25:42.435
Oorah.

1079
01:25:44.320 --> 01:25:45.879
Met Clay Verris there.

1080
01:25:46.680 --> 01:25:49.911
Found something
I was really, really good at.

1081
01:25:51.240 --> 01:25:53.550
Time I left, I had medals on my chest,

1082
01:25:54.320 --> 01:25:58.154
she was gone, and... I had become this.

1083
01:26:00.600 --> 01:26:03.752
You gotta walk away while you still can.

1084
01:26:05.240 --> 01:26:08.358
- This is all I know.
- No, this is all he taught you.

1085
01:26:08.440 --> 01:26:12.229
Stop now,
you can still become something else.

1086
01:26:14.160 --> 01:26:15.309
Sure.

1087
01:26:15.440 --> 01:26:18.432
A doctor? Lawyer?

1088
01:26:18.960 --> 01:26:21.395
Husband. Father.

1089
01:26:21.480 --> 01:26:24.950
All the things this job gives you
the excuse not to be.

1090
01:26:26.680 --> 01:26:28.239
I threw all of that away.

1091
01:26:30.360 --> 01:26:33.159
It'd be a shame to waste these gifts
a second time around.

1092
01:26:38.120 --> 01:26:39.713
I'm sorry, what is your name?

1093
01:26:42.080 --> 01:26:43.434
It's always been Junior.

1094
01:26:44.360 --> 01:26:45.509
Clay Junior.

1095
01:26:47.400 --> 01:26:48.959
I don't really know anymore.

1096
01:26:50.280 --> 01:26:52.396
That's another really good reason to quit.

1097
01:26:59.080 --> 01:27:00.400
You sure about this?

1098
01:27:01.560 --> 01:27:02.914
I need to talk to him.

1099
01:27:04.720 --> 01:27:07.314
So, what happens when we get to him?

1100
01:27:08.160 --> 01:27:09.514
He's not gonna surrender.

1101
01:27:18.280 --> 01:27:19.395
It's him.

1102
01:27:19.480 --> 01:27:20.595
Can I talk to him?

1103
01:27:20.680 --> 01:27:23.240
I want to be the one to tell him
we're all BFFs now.

1104
01:27:24.880 --> 01:27:26.029
Take it.

1105
01:27:27.640 --> 01:27:28.789
This is Junior.

1106
01:27:28.880 --> 01:27:30.234
<i>Are you with Brogan ?</i>

1107
01:27:30.840 --> 01:27:33.036
Why would I be with him?
You sent me to kill him, didn't you?

1108
01:27:33.120 --> 01:27:34.758
<i>Doesn '1' matter. Jusz' run.</i>

1109
01:27:36.920 --> 01:27:37.910
What?

1110
01:27:38.000 --> 01:27:40.196
<i>Run. Getaway from him, now.</i>

1111
01:27:40.280 --> 01:27:42.590
<i>Jun/or, ljusz' Want you safe.</i>

1112
01:27:42.680 --> 01:27:43.715
VVhy?

1113
01:27:43.800 --> 01:27:45.837
Because I'm your favorite experiment?

1114
01:27:45.920 --> 01:27:49.276
<i>N0, because /'m your father
and you need f0 listen to me.</i>

1115
01:27:49.360 --> 01:27:50.430
<i>Run!</i>

1116
01:27:53.080 --> 01:27:54.479
- Get out of the car!
- Go, go!

1117
01:28:00.440 --> 01:28:01.555
Baron!

1118
01:28:02.320 --> 01:28:03.151
No!

1119
01:28:16.160 --> 01:28:17.230
Come on!

1120
01:28:25.760 --> 01:28:27.114
I'm sorry, Henry.

1121
01:28:31.800 --> 01:28:34.269
Move out. Go! Go!

1122
01:28:34.920 --> 01:28:36.672
- Chief Mitchell?
- G0 <i>ahead.</i>

1123
01:28:36.760 --> 01:28:37.750
Clay Verris.

1124
01:28:37.840 --> 01:28:40.354
- I need your units to stand down.
- S/r?

1125
01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:44.991
We're engaging with a terror cell that has
a weaponized biological capability.

1126
01:28:45.080 --> 01:28:47.151
<i>Al/ units, fallback immediate/y.</i>

1127
01:28:49.200 --> 01:28:52.431
Federal authorities have been notified
and are en route.

1128
01:28:52.520 --> 01:28:54.796
<i>Affirmat/ve. Keep me posted, Clay.</i>

1129
01:28:54.880 --> 01:28:55.870
Yes, sir.

1130
01:28:58.240 --> 01:29:00.356
You gotta stand your men down now.

1131
01:29:00.480 --> 01:29:03.199
You did the right thing, Junior,
walking away from him.

1132
01:29:03.280 --> 01:29:05.430
I did what a coward would do.

1133
01:29:05.520 --> 01:29:07.033
Makes rne sick!

1134
01:29:07.120 --> 01:29:08.997
I was asking too much of you.

1135
01:29:09.600 --> 01:29:11.273
I can see that now.

1136
01:29:11.360 --> 01:29:14.716
He deserves better than a missile
shot into his car, Pop.

1137
01:29:14.800 --> 01:29:16.598
It doesn't matter what he deserves.

1138
01:29:16.680 --> 01:29:18.193
He has to die.

1139
01:29:56.960 --> 01:29:59.110
Are you gonna call those goons off now?

1140
01:29:59.200 --> 01:30:00.793
No. But you can.

1141
01:30:01.600 --> 01:30:04.114
Just fire that. Take command.

1142
01:30:05.200 --> 01:30:08.033
Armor is weak at the joints.
Eyes and neck are the kill shots.

1143
01:30:08.520 --> 01:30:09.919
Take right, I take left.

1144
01:30:16.640 --> 01:30:18.119
Muzzle discipline.

1145
01:30:18.200 --> 01:30:20.840
Watch your round count. You set, I spike.

1146
01:30:20.920 --> 01:30:22.319
- Ready?
- Roger that.

1147
01:30:39.880 --> 01:30:40.995
-L'm out.
- Take cover.

1148
01:30:49.440 --> 01:30:50.430
Set!

1149
01:31:02.240 --> 01:31:03.389
Frag out!

1150
01:31:21.760 --> 01:31:25.719
I am trying to make you a man!

1151
01:31:28.160 --> 01:31:29.878
I should've cloned myself.

1152
01:31:37.360 --> 01:31:40.990
"Loving, dedicated, present father."

1153
01:31:43.280 --> 01:31:44.270
Right side!

1154
01:31:49.880 --> 01:31:50.995
Go ahead.

1155
01:31:52.400 --> 01:31:53.390
Do it.

1156
01:32:04.400 --> 01:32:05.799
How many rounds you got left?

1157
01:32:09.440 --> 01:32:10.430
One.

1158
01:32:11.120 --> 01:32:12.315
Okay.

1159
01:32:21.520 --> 01:32:22.715
I'm sorry.

1160
01:32:22.800 --> 01:32:23.870
For what?

1161
01:32:24.440 --> 01:32:25.999
For getting you into this.

1162
01:32:26.080 --> 01:32:27.639
I was the one surveilling you.

1163
01:32:27.720 --> 01:32:28.755
Yeah.

1164
01:32:29.720 --> 01:32:31.791
Anyway, sorry.

1165
01:32:33.360 --> 01:32:34.953
Now let's fight our way out of this thing.

1166
01:33:11.120 --> 01:33:12.599
You're a great partner.

1167
01:33:42.240 --> 01:33:43.310
Thank you.

1168
01:33:43.880 --> 01:33:45.473
Sorry I ran.

1169
01:33:45.560 --> 01:33:47.392
Yeah, well, it's been a rough night.

1170
01:33:47.480 --> 01:33:48.879
How many more out there?

1171
01:33:49.320 --> 01:33:50.515
I didn't see any.

1172
01:33:51.040 --> 01:33:52.075
Verris?

1173
01:33:52.800 --> 01:33:53.915
Out of commission.

1174
01:33:54.920 --> 01:33:56.035
But still alive?

1175
01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:00.070
Yes.

1176
01:34:29.760 --> 01:34:30.750
Here.

1177
01:34:31.280 --> 01:34:33.510
- How bad is that?
-l'm fine.

1178
01:34:35.360 --> 01:34:36.475
You're not.

1179
01:34:38.120 --> 01:34:40.760
Hold the elevated position.
We're gonna secure an out.

1180
01:35:51.760 --> 01:35:52.795
Back off!

1181
01:37:19.400 --> 01:37:20.834
Don't you feel pain?

1182
01:37:52.800 --> 01:37:55.076
I don't know why you're so angry, Henry.

1183
01:38:05.880 --> 01:38:08.269
You were the inspiration for all of this.

1184
01:38:20.480 --> 01:38:22.790
You know where I got the idea?
Are you okay?

1185
01:38:26.160 --> 01:38:27.275
Khafji.

1186
01:38:29.040 --> 01:38:32.351
Watching you go house to house,
wishing I had a whole division of men

1187
01:38:32.440 --> 01:38:33.874
all as good as you.

1188
01:38:34.360 --> 01:38:36.397
Wondering if that could be possible.

1189
01:38:37.480 --> 01:38:38.754
You should be flattered.

1190
01:38:41.680 --> 01:38:43.273
You should be dead.

1191
01:38:43.360 --> 01:38:45.158
You saw what happened over there.

1192
01:38:46.320 --> 01:38:47.833
Atrocities.

1193
01:38:49.840 --> 01:38:52.309
Friends being sent home in a pine box.

1194
01:38:52.400 --> 01:38:55.791
Why should we accept that
if there's a better way?

1195
01:38:59.160 --> 01:39:01.310
And look what we created.

1196
01:39:07.200 --> 01:39:08.679
He's got both of us in him.

1197
01:39:10.400 --> 01:39:14.871
Don't you think your country deserves
a perfect version of you?

1198
01:39:14.960 --> 01:39:17.190
There is no perfect version of me.

1199
01:39:18.280 --> 01:39:20.396
Or him. Or anybody.

1200
01:39:20.480 --> 01:39:21.515
N0?

1201
01:39:22.480 --> 01:39:23.800
He was on his way to Yemen.

1202
01:39:23.880 --> 01:39:27.589
Now, thanks to you, his place is gonna
be taken by someone with parents.

1203
01:39:27.680 --> 01:39:30.672
Someone who feels pain, fear,

1204
01:39:30.760 --> 01:39:32.671
which we had edited out of him.

1205
01:39:32.760 --> 01:39:35.320
Someone with just as many weaknesses

1206
01:39:35.400 --> 01:39:36.993
as the terrorists
that we're trying to kill.

1207
01:39:37.080 --> 01:39:38.559
And you're gonna tell me that's better?

1208
01:39:40.040 --> 01:39:42.554
So why not make a whole army of them?

1209
01:39:42.640 --> 01:39:44.074
Yeah. Why not?

1210
01:39:45.240 --> 01:39:47.834
Think how many American families
we could spare.

1211
01:39:47.960 --> 01:39:50.474
Nobody's son or daughter
would ever have to die.

1212
01:39:50.560 --> 01:39:53.552
No vet comes home with PTSD
and kills himself.

1213
01:39:54.560 --> 01:39:58.599
We can keep the whole world safe
without any actual grief.

1214
01:39:58.720 --> 01:40:00.996
So... who would I be hurting?

1215
01:40:02.160 --> 01:40:04.197
You're talking about people, Clay.

1216
01:40:05.280 --> 01:40:06.395
Henry.

1217
01:40:07.480 --> 01:40:10.313
This is the most humane thing
that Gemini's ever done.

1218
01:40:11.200 --> 01:40:13.476
How many more of me
are running around out there?

1219
01:40:14.880 --> 01:40:16.951
There's only one you, Junior.

1220
01:40:18.840 --> 01:40:20.194
He was a weapon.

1221
01:40:21.240 --> 01:40:22.469
You're my son.

1222
01:40:24.840 --> 01:40:26.194
And I love you...

1223
01:40:27.400 --> 01:40:30.677
as much as any father ever loved any kid.

1224
01:40:35.600 --> 01:40:36.920
I don't have a father.

1225
01:40:38.560 --> 01:40:39.880
Goodbye, Clay.

1226
01:40:39.960 --> 01:40:41.234
Hey, he)'-

1227
01:40:49.200 --> 01:40:51.237
So what the hell are we gonna do, huh?

1228
01:40:52.720 --> 01:40:54.836
Gonna turn him in?
They're not gonna try him.

1229
01:40:54.920 --> 01:40:56.354
They're not gonna shut down his lab.

1230
01:40:57.280 --> 01:40:58.953
We have to end this right now.

1231
01:40:59.040 --> 01:41:00.030
H9)'-

1232
01:41:01.360 --> 01:41:02.589
Look at me.

1233
01:41:04.520 --> 01:41:05.715
Look at me.

1234
01:41:07.360 --> 01:41:08.759
You pull that trigger,

1235
01:41:08.840 --> 01:41:11.559
and you're gonna break something
inside of yourself...

1236
01:41:13.200 --> 01:41:15.237
that'll never get fixed again.

1237
01:41:23.960 --> 01:41:25.075
Don't.

1238
01:41:30.560 --> 01:41:31.675
Let it go.

1239
01:41:32.880 --> 01:41:34.029
Give it to me.

1240
01:41:40.000 --> 01:41:41.673
You don't want those ghosts.

1241
01:41:42.600 --> 01:41:43.829
Trust me.

1242
01:42:23.960 --> 01:42:25.633
You should know better than that.

1243
01:42:27.280 --> 01:42:28.793
Surprised you give a shit.

1244
01:42:30.000 --> 01:42:32.355
Well, we can't be friends anymore.

1245
01:42:33.760 --> 01:42:36.149
Because you did let them try to kill me.

1246
01:42:36.240 --> 01:42:38.959
But doesn't mean I want to see
you drink yourself to death.

1247
01:42:41.400 --> 01:42:43.471
The Gemini lab's been dismantled.

1248
01:42:44.360 --> 01:42:45.953
Cloning program is history.

1249
01:42:48.120 --> 01:42:49.269
And Junior?

1250
01:42:50.160 --> 01:42:51.230
He's untouchable.

1251
01:42:51.800 --> 01:42:53.871
N0 one will bother him, ever.

1252
01:42:55.080 --> 01:42:57.833
And we checked-- There are no more clones.

1253
01:42:58.880 --> 01:43:00.154
What about you?

1254
01:43:01.240 --> 01:43:02.753
IG called.

1255
01:43:02.840 --> 01:43:04.239
I'm looking at charges,

1256
01:43:04.320 --> 01:43:07.551
but if I bury Janet, I can make a deal.

1257
01:43:08.360 --> 01:43:09.998
Well, she earned it.

1258
01:43:14.280 --> 01:43:16.112
I'm really sorry, Henry.

1259
01:43:20.400 --> 01:43:21.629
Take care, Del.

1260
01:43:21.720 --> 01:43:22.835
Yeah, you too.

1261
01:43:23.520 --> 01:43:25.113
And happy retirement.

1262
01:43:55.400 --> 01:43:56.435
H9)'-

1263
01:44:00.480 --> 01:44:01.515
H9)'-

1264
01:44:03.560 --> 01:44:04.914
Good to see you.

1265
01:44:05.000 --> 01:44:06.832
Congrats on the promotion.

1266
01:44:06.920 --> 01:44:08.354
I hear they got big plans.

1267
01:44:08.440 --> 01:44:11.193
Well, after you,
pretty sure I can handle anything.

1268
01:44:12.480 --> 01:44:14.357
- How have you been?
- Good.

1269
01:44:14.440 --> 01:44:17.000
I just settled Baron's estate,

1270
01:44:17.080 --> 01:44:19.071
scattered his ashes in the Caribbean.

1271
01:44:20.200 --> 01:44:23.511
I don't know. All I want to do now
is put some good in the world.

1272
01:44:24.040 --> 01:44:25.553
I just got to figure out how.

1273
01:44:26.440 --> 01:44:27.555
Yeah, you will.

1274
01:44:28.400 --> 01:44:29.674
You sleeping okay?

1275
01:44:30.080 --> 01:44:31.150
Better.

1276
01:44:31.720 --> 01:44:34.280
- No ghosts?
- Not like before.

1277
01:44:34.760 --> 01:44:37.229
Oh, and I actually looked in a mirror
the other day.

1278
01:44:37.320 --> 01:44:39.550
- Really?
- It wasn't horrendous.

1279
01:44:41.400 --> 01:44:42.799
Speaking of mirrors...

1280
01:44:55.880 --> 01:44:57.678
- Catch you later.
- See you later, man.

1281
01:44:58.120 --> 01:44:59.110
H9)'-

1282
01:45:11.960 --> 01:45:12.950
What's this?

1283
01:45:13.040 --> 01:45:14.997
This is you.

1284
01:45:15.120 --> 01:45:18.556
Passport, birth certificate,
driver's license.

1285
01:45:18.640 --> 01:45:20.517
Apparently you got pretty good credit.

1286
01:45:21.960 --> 01:45:23.314
I love the name you chose.

1287
01:45:23.840 --> 01:45:26.070
Jackson? It was my mother's name.

1288
01:45:26.160 --> 01:45:28.356
Hey, she was my mother first.

1289
01:45:28.800 --> 01:45:29.949
Yeah, yeah.

1290
01:45:30.040 --> 01:45:32.031
Don't you "yeah, yeah" rne, young man.

1291
01:45:33.400 --> 01:45:35.357
Come on. I know a great place for lunch.

1292
01:45:39.560 --> 01:45:41.119
So you settled on a major yet?

1293
01:45:41.200 --> 01:45:42.998
Leaning towards engineering.

1294
01:45:43.080 --> 01:45:44.115
Engineering?

1295
01:45:44.920 --> 01:45:47.275
Yeah, you should listen to her.

1296
01:45:47.400 --> 01:45:50.358
If I were you, which I sort of am,

1297
01:45:50.440 --> 01:45:51.794
I'd go with computer science.

1298
01:45:51.880 --> 01:45:54.440
Save that for grad school.
You want to start in humanities.

1299
01:45:54.520 --> 01:45:56.318
- Okay, don't listen to her.
- Don't listen to him.

1300
01:45:56.400 --> 01:45:57.754
You need a grounding in the classics.

1301
01:45:57.840 --> 01:46:00.116
Look, excuse me,
I'm trying to talk with myself here.

1302
01:46:00.200 --> 01:46:02.237
Yeah. You're talking to yourself,
but you're not talking to him.

1303
01:46:02.320 --> 01:46:04.789
Look, I just made a lot of mistakes
when I was young--

1304
01:46:04.920 --> 01:46:07.912
And I'd actually like to make
some of those mistakes myself.

1305
01:46:08.000 --> 01:46:10.355
What I'm trying to say is,
I made them already so you don't have to.

1306
01:46:10.440 --> 01:46:15.116
- Yeah, but he's not you.
- Okay. Everybody, chill the hell out.

1307
01:46:16.800 --> 01:46:18.199
I'm gonna be okay.

1308
01:46:23.280 --> 01:46:24.475
If you're okay...

